In Rust’s `asm!` operand list, explicit register operands must appear at the end, after all positional and named operands.

```rust
unsafe {
    core::arch::asm!(
        "/* {x} */",
        x = in(reg) 5,
        in("eax") 0, // explicit register operand comes last
    );
}
```

Explicit register operands also cannot be referenced with `{}` placeholders; write the register name directly in the assembly template.
